From: Zaurus OS
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: pxa2xx-i2s: don't register PCM ops twice in one rtd

This CPU DAI component and the platform component (pxa2xx-pcm.c) both
register pxa2xx_pcm_ops, and spitz.c names both in its DAI link. The soc
code walks every component in the rtd, so each PCM callback fired twice
per substream: open() requested the DMA channel twice and leaked the first
prtd, close() released the channel twice and kfree()d the same prtd twice.

The platform component owns the ops here, so drop them from the DAI.
---
--- a/sound/soc/pxa/pxa2xx-i2s.c
+++ b/sound/soc/pxa/pxa2xx-i2s.c
@@ -358,11 +358,10 @@
 	.symmetric_rates = 1,
 };
 
+/* no ops/pcm_new/pcm_free on purpose. boards naming both this and
+ * pxa-pcm-audio in one dai link run every pcm callback twice. */
 static const struct snd_soc_component_driver pxa_i2s_component = {
 	.name		= "pxa-i2s",
-	.ops		= &pxa2xx_pcm_ops,
-	.pcm_new	= pxa2xx_soc_pcm_new,
-	.pcm_free	= pxa2xx_pcm_free_dma_buffers,
 };
 
 static int pxa2xx_i2s_drv_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
